# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Added after a real incident: editing files with a script on Windows rewrote
# them CRLF, so a one-line change to CHANGELOG.md showed as the whole file
# rewritten and the actual edit was unreviewable. Without this, whether a diff
# is readable depends on which tool last touched the file.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text and stores it as LF; `eol=lf` keeps
# the working copy LF too, so a Windows editor does not reintroduce CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files git should never try to normalise or diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip binary
*.xcassets binary
